source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Reading: newsletters you chose, as an edition. Read when you like. Newest since your last visit first, the sources you read most on top, and nothing owed: items fade unless you keep them on Later

Usage: mxr reading [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  edition    The edition (the default): since your last visit, earlier this week and fading, with the Later shelf's count
  later      The Later shelf, or put items on it and take them off. Later never fades
  open       Read one item: the issue as reader text, or with --article the article it links to. --article contacts the article's site (named first) unless a copy is saved
  let-go     Let go of items in Reading, or of everything in the edition with --all. Preview with --dry-run; `mxr undo` reverses it
  highlight  Save a passage from an item as a highlight
  export     Every highlight as Markdown (the default) or JSON
  sources    Every source in Reading, best read first, with its fade window and the evidence for unsubscribing
  senders    Reading's inbox mail grouped by sender, as before the edition
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>  Limit to one account; the default covers every account
      --format <FORMAT>    [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help               Print help
